torch's CUDAPluggableAllocator (the .so-based custom allocator API) is the
escape hatch for the one torch memory bug left on gfx803 after the C10_WARP_SIZE
fix. The default caching allocator's block layout can corrupt the next kernel's
access after a GEMM -- silent scattered NaN in an op that reads correctly-written
memory -- reproduced on every ROCm stack (6.4.4/7.14/10.0) with torch's
own elementwise kernels as the victim (no GEMM kernel involved; raw hipMalloc in
the same process is always clean, and a C++ replica of the exact torch pattern is
always clean). A pluggable allocator whose raw allocations come from plain hipMalloc
sidesteps that layout on the stacks where it reproduces: measured on the 7.14 host
with the bmm+add repro, 7/8 rounds corrupt under the default allocator and 0/8
under the hipMalloc-backed pluggable allocator.

NOT a fix to the default allocator -- an opt-in alternative, OFF by default,
enabled only when GFX803_PLUGGABLE_ALLOCATOR is set at runtime (any truthy
value, or a path to the allocator .so; defaults to
/opt/rocm/lib/libgfx803_pluggable.so). See the README's "torch memory:
experimental pluggable allocator" section for usage. Experimental: it changes
allocator semantics globally (every tensor's memory comes from per-allocation
hipMalloc), stats are reported from simple counters, the graphs/IPC/snapshot
parts of the allocator API become no-ops, and it does NOT help on every stack
(verified on 10.0, where the corruption persists even under the pluggable
allocator).

Upstream threw for getDeviceStats/getMemoryFraction/cacheInfo/snapshot/
recordHistory/attachOutOfMemoryObserver -- ComfyUI and other eager frameworks call
memory_stats at startup, so the pluggable allocator crashed the process before it
could serve. This implements those with simple counters tracked in malloc/raw_delete,
and wires the runtime env-var hook into torch.cuda._lazy_init (before _cuda_init,
so the allocator swap happens before anything allocates).

The companion .so is gfx803_pluggable.hip (same directory), built with
hipcc --offload-arch=gfx803 -O2 -fPIC -shared gfx803_pluggable.hip
-o libgfx803_pluggable.so -lamdhip64, installed to /opt/rocm/lib.

